cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and cite the source
  paper listed under "references". This is a draft reference implementation: see
  experiments/results/RESULTS.md for the values it produces and the conditions under which it
  produces them.
title: "federated-privacy-adult: sample-weighted federated averaging with differential privacy on UCI Adult"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Fan
repository-code: "https://github.com/fguo10-tech/federated-privacy-adult"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Draft, reproducible reference implementation of federated learning with differential privacy,
  for researchers who need to train one model across data owners that cannot pool their raw
  data, under an explicit privacy budget, and who want to run, benchmark and extend it. It provides Flower-based
  sample-weighted federated averaging with Opacus DP-SGD and Renyi accounting on the UCI Adult /
  Census Income dataset (1994 U.S. Census extraction), with three workclass-based clients, an
  IID control, centralised and local-only baselines, robust aggregation rules under Byzantine
  clients, a secure-aggregation simulation and an epsilon sweep. Results are reported as a
  Before / After comparison under documented conditions. Every number in the documentation is labelled Paper-reported, Reproduced
  or Target / TBD.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - differential privacy
  - Flower
  - Opacus
  - UCI Adult
  - reproducibility
